largely|mostly|ADVERB|for the most part|To a great extent or for the most part.|chủ yếu; phần lớn|The event was largely organised by volunteers.|Sự kiện chủ yếu do các tình nguyện viên tổ chức.|Modifies a clause, verb phrase, or adjective; largely allows exceptions and does not mean completely.|0
reflection|mirrored-image|NOUN|image seen in a reflective surface|An image of something seen in a mirror or another reflective surface.|hình ảnh phản chiếu|She saw the bridge's reflection in the still water.|Cô ấy thấy hình ảnh cây cầu phản chiếu trong mặt nước phẳng lặng.|Countable; reflection in a surface names the image's location.|0
reflection|careful-thought|NOUN|careful thinking about something|Careful thought about an experience, question, or decision.|sự suy ngẫm; sự cân nhắc|After some reflection, he decided to revise the plan.|Sau khi suy ngẫm, anh ấy quyết định chỉnh sửa kế hoạch.|Usually uncountable for the process; on reflection means after thinking further.|1
tax|required-payment|NOUN|payment required by public authority|Money that a public authority requires people or organizations to pay to fund public services or activities.|thuế|The receipt shows the price and the tax separately.|Biên lai ghi giá và thuế riêng biệt.|Countable for a type or payment, and uncountable in pay tax; no particular rate is implied.|0
tax|charge-tax|VERB|require a tax payment on something|To require a person, income, or transaction to pay tax.|đánh thuế|The fictional city taxes some commercial activities.|Thành phố giả định đánh thuế một số hoạt động thương mại.|Transitive tax a person or activity; the subject is the authority imposing the payment.|1
whoever|any-person|PRONOUN|any person who meets a condition|Any person who does something or meets a stated condition.|bất cứ ai; người nào|Whoever arrives first can choose a seat.|Ai đến trước có thể chọn chỗ ngồi.|Introduces a clause acting as a noun phrase; in formal questions who and whoever have different functions.|0
any|unspecified-amount|DETERMINER|an unspecified amount or even one|Used for an unspecified amount or number, often in a question or negative statement.|nào; chút nào|Have you received any letters this week?|Tuần này bạn có nhận được lá thư nào không?|Before plural count nouns or uncountable nouns in this use; questions and negatives are common, not the only uses of any.|0
any|free-choice|DETERMINER|one chosen without restriction|Used to say that it does not matter which member of a group is chosen.|bất kỳ; bất cứ|You may use any chair in this room.|Bạn có thể dùng bất kỳ chiếc ghế nào trong phòng này.|Before singular or plural count nouns in free-choice use; differs from an unspecified quantity in a question.|-
any|one-unspecified|PRONOUN|one or some without specifying which|One or some members of a group, without naming which.|cái nào; một ít; bất kỳ cái nào|We have spare notebooks if you need any.|Chúng tôi có vở dự phòng nếu bạn cần một ít.|Used without a following noun when the thing is understood; any of plus a defined group is another pronoun construction.|1
any|degree|ADVERB|to even a small extent|To even a small extent, especially with a comparison in a question or negative statement.|chút nào; hơn chút nào|The second attempt was not any easier.|Lần thử thứ hai chẳng dễ hơn chút nào.|Degree adverb before a comparative such as easier or better; does not modify a noun as a determiner here.|2
